  "results": [
    {
      "comments": [
        {
          "commentType": "FUNCTION",
          "texts": [
            {
              "value": "Integrin alpha-2/beta-1 is a receptor for laminin, collagen, collagen C-propeptides, fibronectin and E-cadherin. It recognizes the proline-hydroxylated sequence G-F-P-G-E-R in collagen. It is responsible for adhesion of platelets and other cells to collagens, modulation of collagen and collagenase gene expression, force generation and organization of newly synthesized extracellular matrix"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "commentType": "FUNCTION",
          "texts": [
